// COMPLIANCE / disclosure vertical — given a company's zero-padded SEC CIK,
// Orbital fetches its legal name, SIC industry and MOST-RECENT filing (SEC EDGAR).
// Same router, a new public-disclosure domain (joins the company brain by legal name).
//
// Example: Apple Inc. — CIK 0000320193.
// NOTE: EDGAR keys on the CIK, not the ticker. There is no by-ticker endpoint;
// resolving AAPL -> 0000320193 needs a full scan of company_tickers.json (see
// the ticker -> CIK caveat in build/gov-uk/taxi/edgar.taxi).
// CAVEAT: SEC requires a descriptive User-Agent header on every request
// ("company-brain demo jhammant@gmail.com") or it returns HTTP 403.
given { cik : markets.edgar.SecCik = "0000320193" }
find { markets.edgar.EdgarSubmissions }
